Last good working version without upstream sockets handling: Titan v8.
Current version with upstream sockets handling (forced disconnec) -> Titan v11.
When v8 is forced to stop (ctrl+c) , rm.datakom.com.tr keeps showing controllers connected (=upstream socket remained open).
When v11 is forced to stop, immediately rm showing controllers disconnected (=upstream socket forcilby closed )
Moreover in V11 when we kill (disconnect) an ID the corresponding upstream socket is killed as well.
Titan Bug V11 - /autodisconnectoldest -> it will fail in case from the same IP more controllers are connected ..... since this routine is grouping connections purely
based on their IP.....
